  "headlines": [
    "API key is the most common auth method: 51 of 100 apps (51%) support it. OAuth2 follows with 48.",
    "47 of 100 apps (47%) are self-serve (instant, free tier or trial); 31 (31%) are gated by a paid plan, an approval or review step, or sales; for 22 (22%) the sources did not establish how access works.",
    "Most open category: Productivity and Project Management (8/10 self-serve). Most gated: Marketing, Ads, Email and Social (5/10 gated).",
    "The most common named blocker is 'paid plan' (15 apps; 16 more are tagged 'other').",
    "38 apps can be built into an agent toolkit today with no external gate; 32 are conditional; 16 need outreach; 14 remain unclear after verification.",
    "Official MCP servers exist for 61 apps; 4 have community-only MCP.",
    "Composio already ships a toolkit for 79 of 100 apps; 7 build-now apps have no Composio toolkit yet (the most actionable gaps).",
    "Where a toolkit exists, its auth schemes fully match our finding for 34 of 79 apps (independent cross-check)."
  ],
